405	     3	/// Switch by Speaker's one reader (spec §11 SW-20, SW-25), shaped like
406	     4	/// `AudioSync.read`: the edited project's snapshot and plan, and each
407	     5	/// microphone's loudness and speech caches, read onto the range's 10 ms grid
408	     6	/// through `ClipLevelSeries`. A missing cache file is "still being analysed",
409	     7	/// never silence. In the faces mode (SW8) it also reads each face speaker's
410	     8	/// angle through `readFaces` (`SpeakerSwitch+Faces.swift`).
411	     9	extension SpeakerSwitch {
412	    10	    /// `clips` nil: the document's selection. `pairing` nil: SW-20's
413	    11	    /// defaults. `range` nil: the In–Out range, else the selected angle
414	    12	    /// clips' extent. nil only when the edited project's plan cannot be read.
415	    13	    static func read(
416	    14	        from document: ProjectDocument, clips: [UInt32]?, pairing: Pairing?,
