551	     3	/// Who speaks when, as `reframe_clip {follow: speaker}` is handed it (road map
552	     4	/// "creator-jobs" VR6a, spec §11 VR-60 (c)): SW-21's labels and SW-22 (a)–(e)
553	     5	/// read exactly as `shots` reads them, but on the labels themselves, not on
554	     6	/// angles, so the framing and Switch by Speaker agree about who is talking.
555	     7	///
556	     8	/// - the crosstalk bridge and the nobody bridge (`bridgedRuns`, SW-22 (a));
557	     9	/// - a person run of at least `minTurn` starts that microphone's turn, a
558	    10	///   crosstalk run of at least `crosstalkMin` one turn per microphone active
559	    11	///   at any of its crosstalk steps; nobody and shorter runs hold;
560	    12	/// - each start at `snap(onset − lead)`, never before the last start or the
561	    13	///   range's start; the first start is the range's start;
562	    14	/// - each turn ends at the next start, the last at the range's end, so the
563	    15	///   turns tile the range (crosstalk turns share one span).
564	    16	///
565	    17	/// Pure (SW-25): reads no document, file or clock.
